WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.334 --> 00:00:03.084
(keyboard music)

00:00:05.726 --> 00:00:06.559
- [Stevo] It's the perfect day.

00:00:06.559 --> 00:00:07.508
You know what I'm talking about?

00:00:07.508 --> 00:00:09.777
It's the perfect day to just go outside,

00:00:09.777 --> 00:00:11.624
and do stuff with your friends.

00:00:11.624 --> 00:00:12.859
Or friend.

00:00:12.859 --> 00:00:14.987
Your human friend, your animal friend,

00:00:14.987 --> 00:00:16.305
doesn't really matter.

00:00:16.305 --> 00:00:17.138
Does it?

00:00:17.138 --> 00:00:18.373
My friend Shabby,

00:00:18.373 --> 00:00:20.174
is an African Sulcata tortoise,

00:00:20.174 --> 00:00:22.100
but she's from Southern California,

00:00:22.100 --> 00:00:22.933
which is funny.

00:00:22.933 --> 00:00:24.958
Sometimes if one of us is feeling blue,

00:00:24.958 --> 00:00:25.870
we'll just go to the park,

00:00:25.870 --> 00:00:27.120
and we'll hang.

00:00:28.017 --> 00:00:30.187
We decided to try yoga for the first time.

00:00:30.187 --> 00:00:34.279
So we found some mats, and
we got our downward dog on.

00:00:34.279 --> 00:00:36.491
Or, at least tried to.

00:00:36.491 --> 00:00:37.324
I mean tried to,

00:00:37.324 --> 00:00:39.732
so I don't think Shabby
was feeling it too much.

00:00:39.732 --> 00:00:41.355
After working up an appetite,

00:00:41.355 --> 00:00:43.886
I got us a croissant from the cafe.

00:00:43.886 --> 00:00:45.976
I wasn't too into it though,

00:00:45.976 --> 00:00:47.496
and I don't think Shabby was either.

00:00:47.496 --> 00:00:48.567
So we went ahead,

00:00:48.567 --> 00:00:51.144
and we just fed it to
one of the local ducks.

00:00:51.144 --> 00:00:51.977
Between you and me,

00:00:51.977 --> 00:00:53.716
I think Shabby has
something against ducks,

00:00:53.716 --> 00:00:55.643
but I think they're fine,

00:00:55.643 --> 00:00:56.859
so whatever.

00:00:56.859 --> 00:00:58.155
Sometimes in friendship,

00:00:58.155 --> 00:00:59.645
there's these differences

00:00:59.645 --> 00:01:01.614
that you discover about each other.

00:01:01.614 --> 00:01:05.056
They could seem a little
bit irreconcilable.

00:01:05.056 --> 00:01:05.889
At one point,

00:01:05.889 --> 00:01:06.861
Shabby's lack of interest

00:01:06.861 --> 00:01:08.180
in some of the things we were doing,

00:01:08.180 --> 00:01:09.738
just got me so heated,

00:01:09.738 --> 00:01:11.220
that I just split,

00:01:11.220 --> 00:01:14.279
and went and chilled with
some of the birds at the park.

00:01:14.279 --> 00:01:15.921
Or I tried to.

00:01:15.921 --> 00:01:19.265
But none of them seemed to wanna
build a friendship with me.

00:01:19.265 --> 00:01:20.098
That's cool.

00:01:20.098 --> 00:01:21.982
That's totally fine.

00:01:21.982 --> 00:01:24.269
Luckily true friends take you back.

00:01:24.269 --> 00:01:26.238
Even after you've thrown a fit.

00:01:26.238 --> 00:01:27.674
And it's a good thing,

00:01:27.674 --> 00:01:30.068
because when you've had the perfect day,

00:01:30.068 --> 00:01:32.112
you know there can be no catch.

00:01:32.112 --> 00:01:33.126
There's only love,

00:01:33.126 --> 00:01:35.113
and that's more than enough,

00:01:35.113 --> 00:01:37.059
I get that I'm not cut out for everyone,

00:01:37.059 --> 00:01:39.996
which is probably why my
only friend is a tortoise.

00:01:39.996 --> 00:01:43.492
Who can't hear me. (laughing)

